      "translatedText": "| Syntax | Description | Notes |\n|:---|:---|:---|\n| `_1` | The first parameter passed when calling a new function | From `std::placeholders` |\n| `_2` | The second parameter passed when calling a new function | Can be used to adjust the order |\n| Fixed value | Written directly in `bind` parameter | By default, it is copied and saved |\n| `&Class::method` | Member function pointer | An object still needs to be bound afterward |\n| `this` | The current object pointer inside a member function | Often used as the second parameter when binding a member function |\n| `std::ref(x)` | Bind by reference `x` | If not written, `std::ref` is usually copied |",
